<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yusuf al-Mutaman ibn Hud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1085">1085</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as al-Mu'tamin, Yusuf al-Mu'taman ibn Hud</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yusuf al-Mutaman ibn Hud was the Hudid king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> from 1081 to 1085, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-al-muqtadir">Ahmad I al-Muqtadir</a>. A mathematician, he wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kitob">Kitab</a> al-Istikmal, a large treatise on geometry studied in later centuries. During his reign Rodrigo Díaz, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-cid">El Cid</a>, served Zaragoza and defeated its enemies, including Aragon and the Taifa of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Lérida</a>.</p></div>
